   "daf": "32a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "וְעוֹרוֹת לְבוּבִין. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: אֵיזֶהוּ עוֹר לָבוּב? כָּל שֶׁקָּרוּעַ כְּנֶגֶד הַלֵּב וְקָדוּר כְּמִין אֲרוּבָּה, יֵשׁ עָלָיו קוֹרֶט דָּם — אָסוּר.",
   "en": "§ The mishna further teaches: «And hides» with a tear opposite the «heart» are prohibited. «The Sages taught: What is» considered «a hide» with a tear opposite the «heart? Any» hide «that is torn opposite the heart and incised» in a shape «similar to an aperture,» and which «has a trace of» coagulated «blood on it,» is «prohibited.»"
  }
 ],
